course: dictionary
lesson: 7115
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word pee is one of them. Pee can be a verb (to pee), a noun (a pee, or pee itself), and the name of a letter. You can tell which meaning is meant by reading the words around it. «Do you need a pee?» means you might need to go to the toilet.
explain: Pee is informal, which means it is the everyday, relaxed way of speaking. At school or at the doctor's, people often say «urinate» or «go to the toilet» instead. Knowing this helps you choose the right word for the place you are writing in.
explain: Look at the clues. «Pale yellow pee usually means you are drinking enough water» uses pee as a noun for urine, the liquid the body gets rid of. In «The letter P sounds like pee», the word is about a sound and a letter, not the body. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
fact: Pee is informal, so at school or at the doctor's, people often say «urinate» or «go to the toilet».
fact: As a verb, the forms are pee, pees, peed and peeing.
fact: «Pee» can also mean urine, the liquid your body gets rid of.
fact: Pale yellow pee usually means you are drinking enough water.
fact: «Pee» is also the name of the letter P.
exercise: «Do you need a pee?» What does pee mean here? | A small bird that sings | *A trip to the toilet | To shout very loudly
exercise: «Pale yellow pee usually means you are drinking enough water.» What does this suggest? | You have been swimming all day | You have eaten too many sweets | *You are drinking enough water | You need to sleep
exercise: Which meaning of pee is the name of a letter? | *P | K | B | T
test: «Bears can go months without eating, drinking, peeing or pooing.» In this sentence, peeing means? | Climbing up a tree root | Sleeping in a den | *Letting urine out of the body | Eating honey from a tree
test: Which word would a doctor or teacher probably use instead of pee? | *Urinate | Splash | Yawn | Sneeze
exam: Which meaning fits pee in «Pale yellow pee usually means you are drinking enough water»? | A type of tree | To go to the toilet, as a verb | The letter P | *Urine, the liquid the body gets rid of
